    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "fore, we could not claim the merit of saints, though we did not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "enjoy pleasures सोढाः—We had to put up with the inclemencies",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of the weather &c. on account of poverty (as Râmarshi suggests)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "but that does not entitle us to the merit of penance. ध्यातं—We",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "were engaged in contemplation, not of the feet of S'iva but of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "wealth Thus though we did the same actions that are done by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "sages, viz forgiving, renunciation, endurance, and contemplation,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "as to the fruits of those actions we have been deceived. We",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "went the wrong way, and hence our disappointment. For निय-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "मितप्राणैन शम्भोः पदं cf अन्तर्यश्च मुमुक्षुभिर्नियमितप्राणादिभिर्मृग्यते Vik,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "I. 1 The fig is विशेषोक्ति.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 8. वयमेव भुक्ताः— desire ( which was never satisfied ) has",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "preyed on our minds ( like canker on a bud ). Some supply",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कालेन but that idea is expressed in याताः. तप्ताः—i. e. with cares",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and anxieties. वयमेव याताः-our bodies have been wasted away; or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "it is we (men) that have had our exits. In popular language we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "say that time passes; but really speaking it is not time that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "passes; time is eternal; but we have our exits from this world.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "तृष्णा न जीर्णा —cf next sl. ०जीर्णा weakened by old age.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl 9 All parts of the body indicate the advent of old age.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Greed alone grows young, i. e., though old we feel as greedy as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "when we were young, or even more. आक्रान्तं-Over-ridden; on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "which a footing has been made by पलितं—gray hair: पलितं जरसा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "शौक्ल्यं Amara. तृष्णा here may also be taken as an उपलक्षण i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "indicating kindred things—the feelings of the mind. तरुणायते—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "तरुणी इवाचरति is young Cf. जीर्यन्ते जीर्यतः केशा दन्ता जीर्यन्ति जीर्यतः ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "जीर्यतश्चक्षुषी श्रोत्रे तृष्णैका तरुणायते Pt. V. 16.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "In line 5, the 'A' of 'Amara.' is partially missing/broken."
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 10. पुरुषबहुमानः—Râmarshi explains this as equivalent",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "to पुरुषसम्बन्धी पुरुषाणां यूनां यो भवतीत्यर्थः, which is equivalent to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "पुरुषत्वविषयकः: another way is to take it as पुरुषेषु बहुमानः respect",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "among men. The first is preferable. समानाः-of equal age or rank;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "contemporary. जीवितसमाः—equal to life, valued or esteemed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "as life itself. The other interpretation placed on this viz.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "जीवितं समं पूर्णं येषां can hardly be acceptable. स्वर्—The word is an",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
